{"duration_api_ms":222247,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d2206194-f974-45f9-84fb-3005b5c5774a","total_cost_usd":0.273722,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14487,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":21577,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":16157},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14487,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":21577,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14487,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14487},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":21577,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14487,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.273722,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":16157,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"All 9 feasible non-dominated points sit on one line at D≈3.36-3.38 m, bluntness 1.25, cone 70° (both at their bounds or near a limit), and differ only in flight-path angle. Three constraints pin the corner. Peak g is about 12 (margin 0.00398 at 11.952 g) and sets the steepest FPA of about -3.57. Heatshield mass fraction sets D at about 3.388 m. The geometry limit sets bluntness at about 1.29 for cone 70°. The front spans q of 247-290 kW/m2 and T of 393-418 K. Against the 2.5 MW/m2 and 450 K reference, hypervolume gains now come from small shifts in T and q, or from extending or densifying the front.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-90fa3c4a7771 (FPA -3.57, D 3.38) has g margin 0.00398. C-cb4f7a3f0bb6 to C-90fa3c4a7771 gives about 1.65 g/deg, so FPA -3.59 should still give about 11.985 g. The g effect of D is small: about +0.4 g per m.\",\"Mass margin is linear in D (about -0.587/m): 0.01636 at 3.36, 0.01049 at 3.37, 0.004613 at 3.38, and -0.001285 at 3.39 (C-02b4b3f7ed6c, infeasible). It also rises by about 0.029 per unit bluntness (C-654d5bc175c0 vs C-90fa3c4a7771). D≈3.387-3.388 is therefore still feasible.\",\"At D 3.35 and FPA -3.55, bluntness 1.15 vs 1.25 gives q 298.1k vs 293.4k and T 394.68 vs 394.09 (C-9d7623ea4b37 vs C-5066d206f4ce). Higher bluntness is better on both objectives, and g is unaffected.\",\"C-f46ea12b9a86 (bluntness 1.3, cone 70) fails with a -12 mm fore-cone length, while 1.25 works. The bluntness limit at cone 70° is therefore near 1.29, so 1.27-1.28 is probably buildable.\",\"D sensitivity at FPA -3.55: q falls about 1.25k and T about 0.18 K per +0.01 m (C-5066d206f4ce, C-56e677f2754b, C-cb4f7a3f0bb6).\",\"The front has gaps between FPA -1.7 and -3.0 (C-b8f1cf89702a, C-6d99358fc11d, C-a708631e3a6a, C-7a42d9b2504a, C-71dbb7df9fb4). FPA is bounded at -1.5 and has not been tried below -1.7.\",\"Points far from the corner (C-7e930f570744, C-0a0993b4b67b, C-f1dfaff79f31) are either infeasible on g or dominated.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Heat flux scales roughly as sqrt(rho/Rn) V^3, and bondline temperature follows the integrated heat load. A larger D and nose radius and a lower ballistic coefficient move peak heating higher in the atmosphere. A steeper FPA shortens the heating pulse and lowers T, but raises q and peak g. Peak g depends almost only on FPA and V, not on ballistic coefficient. So g fixes the steepest FPA, mass fraction fixes D, and geometry fixes bluntness and cone. The remaining moves are to push D and bluntness to their limits, hold FPA just inside the g limit, and cover the trade-off curve uniformly, including the shallow end near -1.5.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Bluntness 1.27-1.28 at cone 70° may fail the geometry check, since the exact limit is extrapolated from one failure (about 1.29). The g margin at FPA -3.585 to -3.59 is only 0.001-0.003 of the limit, so small model error could make those points infeasible. Extrapolating to FPA -1.5 and the sensitivities to D and bluntness are linear approximations. The effect of cone angle below 70° is barely characterised and is only probed once. My g slope and geometry threshold are inferences from the data, not known simulator internals.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-b8f1cf89702a\",\"rationale\":\"Extend the front to the shallow FPA bound of -1.5 at D 3.38, which is mass-feasible (margin 0.0046). This adds a new low-q end point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":421.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the front extends left cheaply; g is about 9.1, so it is well inside the limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6d99358fc11d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the shallow end of the front at FPA -1.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":245300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":419.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front between -1.5 and -1.7.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6d99358fc11d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front gap between FPA -1.7 and -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.85},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":248900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Interpolates a smooth front; a cheap coverage gain.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6d99358fc11d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front gap between FPA -2.0 and -2.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":254600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Coverage of the trade-off curve.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6d99358fc11d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front gap between FPA -2.3 and -2.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Coverage of the trade-off curve.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6d99358fc11d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front gap between FPA -2.6 and -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Coverage of the trade-off curve.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6d99358fc11d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front gap between FPA -3.0 and -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":279600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Coverage of the trade-off curve.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cb4f7a3f0bb6\",\"rationale\":\"Push FPA slightly steeper than the current -3.57 limit. Estimated g is about 11.985, still under 12.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.59},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":290700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.16,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the g slope and whether the corner extends by about 0.2 K in T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly higher bluntness (1.27) with D 3.386 (predicted mass margin about 0.0017). Both changes lower q and T together.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.27,\"diameter_m\":3.386,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the bluntness geometry limit and the corner gain; if it works, the whole front can shift.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Aggressive corner: bluntness 1.28, D 3.388 (mass margin about 0.0008), FPA -3.585 (g about 11.98).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.28,\"diameter_m\":3.388,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.585},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the bluntness geometry limit (about 1.29) and the mass and g margins together; one of the best possible corner points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the mid-front point at FPA -3.3 to bluntness 1.27 and D 3.387.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.27,\"diameter_m\":3.387,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":281500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.87,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Would dominate C-fe378e1d3bfd if the D and bluntness benefits are additive.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the mid-front point at FPA -3.0 to bluntness 1.27 and D 3.387.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.27,\"diameter_m\":3.387,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Would dominate C-71dbb7df9fb4 if the benefits are additive.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the mid-front point at FPA -2.6 to bluntness 1.27 and D 3.387.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.27,\"diameter_m\":3.387,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.07,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Would dominate C-7a42d9b2504a if the benefits are additive.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the shallow-mid front point at FPA -2.0 to bluntness 1.27 and D 3.387.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.27,\"diameter_m\":3.387,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Would dominate C-6d99358fc11d if the benefits are additive.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow end at FPA -1.5 with bluntness 1.28 and D 3.388, aiming for the lowest possible q.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.28,\"diameter_m\":3.388,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":241600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":420.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front to the lowest q, and tests 1.28 bluntness for buildability.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow-mid point at FPA -1.8 with bluntness 1.28 and D 3.388.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.28,\"diameter_m\":3.388,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":245800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds another look at bluntness 1.28 on the shallow side, so one geometry failure does not decide the question.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9d7623ea4b37\",\"rationale\":\"Exploratory probe of cone angle below 70° (68° with bluntness 1.1 and D 3.34) to gauge the cone effect on q, T and mass margin. Expected to be dominated.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"diameter_m\":3.34},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":302000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cone angle is nearly unexplored in the good region, and the mass-margin sensitivity to it is unknown.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.27, D 3.387, FPA -3.59: a tight-g corner variant.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.27,\"diameter_m\":3.387,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.59},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.92,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the combined g, mass and bluntness margins; g is about 11.988, with only about 0.1% margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-90fa3c4a7771\",\"rationale\":\"Push D only to 3.385 (mass margin about 0.0017) at the current FPA -3.57. A safe incremental corner gain with no geometry risk.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.27,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Confirms the linear D sensitivity and gives a guaranteed small improvement.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":180205,"type":"result","duration_ms":222283,"uuid":"eff56091-f9e8-4b65-9577-6d6cbb4db278","ttft_stream_ms":1163,"time_to_request_ms":33,"first_content_frame_ms":1163,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
